  "reason": "The study reports a model for inferring host species and cross-species transmission of Staphylococcus aureus based on genomic data. While it mentions classification accuracy (98%) and prediction of origin for isolates from livestock-exposed workers (97.5%), it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results in the context of intervention efficacy or outcomes. The focus is on pathogen host prediction, not on the translation of research findings from animals to humans for therapeutic purposes."
